<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12511" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποδοκεῖ</span></b> , impers., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοκέω</span>) mostly c. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή</span> et
			inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέδοξέ σφι μὴ
			τιμωρέειν</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>it seemed good</i> to them
				<i>not</i> to do, they <i>resolved not . .,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.152
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεί σφι ἀ. μὴ ἐπιδιώκειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					8.111
				</span></i>
			; without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				2.3.9
			</span></i>: sts. with inf. omitted, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥς σφι ἀπέδοξε</span> when they <i>resolved not</i>
			(to go on), when they <i>changed their mind,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.172
			</span></i>.</div>
